  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Port the bounded native EPA algorithm and composed GJK/EPA diagnostics with independent penetration witnesses.",
  "regressions": [
    "Fourteen live Rust fixtures exercise all 49 convex shape pairs over seven separation/rotation profiles, empty inputs, partial workgroups, strided rows and the explicit zero-dimensional point-touch fallback.",
    "Composed GJK/EPA catches sensitivity to valid but numerically different GJK simplexes; change 0042 fixes the reproduced native zero-depth bug.",
    "Validation rejects invalid shape witnesses, penetration vectors, normals, statuses and guards, while accepting valid tangential witness changes and opposite normals for proven coincident symmetric shapes."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Nonunique contact points use independent shape containment and penetration-vector proofs; normals, depth and dual support gaps remain tightly compared. This is not a global float tolerance increase.",
    "The native private EPA source is linked directly into the CPU oracle, with mutable-reference noalias disabled.",
    "A separate silhouette-expansion macro avoids the Python compiler static nesting limit without changing the native loop order or capacities.",
    "The EPA arrays are per-thread private storage; Ascend source lowering cannot qualify vendor resource limits."
  ],
  "related_changes": [
    "0042-epa-origin-roundoff",
    "0041-convex-support-gjk"
  ]
}
